WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.380
A Bash script should invoke curl in a way that is easy to review and test.

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:18.280
The executable, stable options, URL, headers, method, payload source, output destination, timeout, and retry behavior should be visible as separate parts of the request design.

3
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.800
Avoid building one large curl command string from variable data.

4
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:29.540
Command strings are difficult to review because they mix data, options, quoting rules, and shell syntax.

5
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.400
They also tempt later re-parsing, which makes it harder to prove what curl will actually receive.

6
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.120
Arrays are useful for curl options and operands.

7
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:46.660
A script can define fixed options, append validated optional values, and pass the array while preserving argument boundaries.

8
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:52.840
This approach is clearer than manually adding quotes inside a generated command line.

9
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.520
Quote values that should remain literal.

10
00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:08.020
URLs, header values, file paths, output paths, request data values, and method names should not accidentally split into multiple arguments or become shell syntax.

11
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:14.520
Validation decides whether a value is allowed; quoting and arrays preserve the value during invocation.

12
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:23.920
Inputs that affect methods, headers, files, timeouts, redirects, retries, and output locations should be validated before curl runs.

13
00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:28.820
A target environment label can map to a known API base URL.

14
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.960
A supported method can be selected from a small set.

15
00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:36.060
A download path can be checked against approved directories.

16
00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:39.620
The goal is a request that another engineer can inspect.

17
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:49.560
If the script makes clear which options are fixed, which values vary, and what validation protects them, curl automation becomes easier to maintain and safer to operate.
